aseline_applied_mm":0.0,"recommended_applied_mm":0.0,"depletion_end_mm":3.2489999999999997}],"assumptions":["Simulated, not your confirmed actions: every day in the window is replayed by the engine, not recorded from anything you did.","The baseline is your saved schedule applied in full on every scheduled day; schedule days are spread evenly from your last watering date.","The replay uses the same engine, cited constants, skip threshold, efficiency and application cap as a live recommendation.","A backtest has no historical forecast, so each scheduled day is decided from the depletion at the start of that day instead of a projected horizon.","The window starts at the refill point, the same convention the live recommendation uses before a recorded watering.","Rain and ET₀ are observed gridded Open-Meteo values for your coordinates, not measurements in your yard.","Estimated water avoided = baseline volume − simulated recommended volume. It is an estimate, not a metered saving.","GreenFlow provides irrigation advice. It does not control or modify your irrigation timer."],"limitations":["Observed weather only removes water the engine would have skipped; it cannot replay a forecast the way the live page does.","The schedule is your reported frequency, not a log of when the sprinkler ran.","No flow meter, water bill, or soil-moisture sensor is used."],"sources":[{"id":"open-meteo-history","label":"Weather history used","citation":"Open-Meteo forecast API, daily past_days: observed precipitation_sum and et0_fao_evapotranspiration (FAO-56 reference evapotranspiration).","url":"https://open-meteo.com/"},{"id":"fao56-table-12","label":"Kc","citation":"FAO-56 Table 12, p. 112: cool-season turfgrass Kc mid 0.95; warm-season turfgrass Kc mid 0.85 (footnote 15).","url":"https://www.fao.org/4/x0490e/x0490e0b.htm"},{"id":"fao56-table-22","label":"Depletion fraction","citation":"FAO-56 Table 22, p. 165: turfgrass depletion fraction p = 0.40 (cool season) and p = 0.50 (warm season)